# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# What the screen says on Curse of the Azure Bonds with every highlight
# a block (#588; text-create.leg is Pool of Radiance's): the screen read
# back in the program's own font (machine/screen_text.h) through the
# title's bar, the main menu and a character's creation, with
# `modern-controls` on. A selection is then a block with a margin, a
# cell that is not a glyph in two colours until its column 0 and row 7
# are blanked out (`docs/hosts.md` §10), and that second reading is what
# this holds: the lit word of a bar, the lit row of a list and the main
# menu's cursor each come back as their own characters, black on white.
# Each `text` line holds one still's screen text - every cell's
# character, ink and paper - to the digest the program's own output had
# when this leg was driven. The text itself is the program's and is not
# here.
#
# Driven on the Steam copy with its shipped slots (`curse-slots`), on
# `tests/sessions/curse-name-arrows.rec`'s keys as far as the icon.
# `--wall none` makes the roll the same roll every run. With the seam
# off the title's bar and the race list read back byte for byte as they
# do here, 41 and 84 pixels apart: the program's own highlight is the
# same black on white without the margin.

about the screen read back as text over Curse's block highlights, through character creation
kind single
program START.EXE
speed 386
seam modern-controls
until 182951200
every 50

# The challenge, which takes any letter; CREATE; Down to the second race;
# the first gender; Down, Up, Down to the second class; the first
# alignment; the roll kept; a name with the four arrows among its
# letters, which type nothing; and out of the icon editor.
key P@2500
key A@2650
key Return@2800
key C@2950
key Down@3400
key Return@3550
key Return@4000
key Down@4450
key Up@4600
key Down@4750
key Return@4900
key Return@5350
key N@5950
key T@6550
key Right@6700
key O@6850
key Up@7000
key R@7150
key Down@7300
key K@7450
key Left@7600
key Return@7750
key E@8500

